// Generic combat signals consumed by weapon-perk reactions (WeaponPerkReactionSystem) - separate
// from Enemy.qtn's own OnEnemyDied/OnEnemyKnockedBack since those are Enemy-specific and don't
// carry an owner. Dispatched from DamageUtility.ApplyDamage; source lets a consumer ignore a
// kill/crit/hit that didn't come from a weapon (a skill, an environment hazard) without a second
// lookup.

signal OnEntityKilled(EntityRef target, EntityRef owner, DamageSource source);

signal OnCriticalHit(EntityRef target, EntityRef owner, FP damage, DamageSource source);

// Narrower sibling of OnCriticalHit - fired additionally (not instead) only when this same crit was
// also flagged isExplosion:true in DamageUtility.ApplyDamage. Doesn't extend OnCriticalHit's own
// signature (that would ripple into every existing subscriber - Flashpoint, weapon perks, Rift
// Mutations) - a dedicated signal is purely additive instead. See Pixie's Volatile Payload
// (docs: Heroes/Pixie/DemolitionMastery.qtn).
signal OnExplosionCriticalHit(EntityRef target, EntityRef owner, FP damage, DamageSource source);

// Fired once per genuine radius explosion - not per target caught in it, see OnHealthDamageApplied
// above for that shape instead. Only from the two real explosion sources, AreaHitData.Detonate
// (bomb-type) and HitEffectUtility.ApplyExplosion (weapon-perk-type) - deliberately never fired from
// ExplodeOnDestroyUtility.TryDetonate (a Mini Bomb's own detonation), so a Mini Bomb dropped by
// Pixie's Pocket Bombs trait can never generate another one - see that trait's own comment.
signal OnAreaExplosionDetonated(EntityRef owner, FPVector3 center, FP radius, DamageSource source);

// Fired from DamageUtility.ApplyDamage whenever damage actually lands on Health/Shield (i.e. the
// post-Armor/Shield-split amount is > 0) - unlike OnWeaponHitLanded below, NOT gated to
// DamageSource.Weapon, so it fires for every source including None (environmental). owner may be
// EntityRef.None - a consumer that needs a valid attacker (e.g. Max's Vendetta) must check that
// itself, same as every other owner-carrying signal in this file. directHit is false when this call
// is a DoT/status-tick replay (ApplyDamage's own bypassOutgoingResolution) - lets a consumer
// distinguish a live hit from a burn/poison tick reusing an already-resolved magnitude. See
// docs/max-vendetta-fire-mastery.md's "Health-vs-Shield damage reporting" section.
signal OnHealthDamageApplied(EntityRef target, EntityRef owner, FP amount, DamageSource source, Boolean directHit);

// Shield counterpart to OnHealthDamageApplied - fired for the portion Shield actually absorbed,
// before Health is touched. Same directHit semantics.
signal OnShieldDamageApplied(EntityRef target, EntityRef owner, FP amount, DamageSource source, Boolean directHit);

// Fired on every landed hit (not just a kill or a crit) whose source is a weapon - what actually
// advances Weapon's shared ramp pool (RampStacks, see Weapon.qtn) for Suppressive Cycle/Overcharge
// Cycle/Relentless Fire. target added for Fracture Rounds (WeaponPerkReactionSystem.
// OnWeaponHitLanded) - the ramp pool itself still only reads owner.
signal OnWeaponHitLanded(EntityRef target, EntityRef owner);
